{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0007656","label":"Gerstmann-Straussler-Scheinker syndrome","definition":"A very rare and fatal disorder of spongiform encephalopathy usually caused by mutations of the prion protein (PRNP) gene. It is characterized by the accumulation of amyloid in the brain. Signs and symptoms include lack of motor coordination, unsteady gait, and difficulty walking. As the disease progresses, patients develop speech difficulties and dementia.","synonyms":["GSD","Gerstmann Straussler Scheinker syndrome","Gerstmann-Straussler disease","Gerstmann-Straussler-Scheinker disease","amyloidosis cerebral with spongiform encephalopathy","cerebellar ataxia, progressive dementia, and amyloid deposits in the central nervous system","encephalopathy subacute spongiform Gerstmann-Straussler type","prion dementia"],"xrefs":["DOID:4249","GARD:0007690","ICD10CM:A81.82","ICD9:046.71","MEDGEN:4886","MESH:C535800","MedDRA:10072075","NANDO:1200190","NCIT:C84727","NORD:0007656","OMIM:137440","Orphanet:356","SCTID:67155006","UMLS:C0017495","icd11.foundation:406818835"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":5,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":39,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_b4a2603785d6","source":"MONDO:0007656","target":"PRNP","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:356","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/356","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) in (Assessed) — prion protein (Kanno blood group)"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:137440","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://omim.org/entry/137440","snippet":"PRNP is annotated as disease gene of OMIM:137440 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, OMIM-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["OMIM","Orphanet"],"level":"curated"}],"phenotypes":[{"edge":{"id":"e_76cf9ca43d42","sou